Subject: How to code NIL genotype in R/qtl?
Message-ID: <egc2GltlKfs.QeOxue0XCAAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl-disc/c/egc2GltlKfs/m/QeOxue0XCAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello,

I have NIL (near isogenic lines) with me to conduct quality control with R/qtl. But I don't know how to code for the genotype. Can R/qtl handle NIL lines and how can I code for the recurrent alleles and donor allele?

Ant light you can shed on this issue will be much appreciated.

Thanks!

Catherine

From u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com  Mon Sep 30 20:27:17 2019
From: u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com (Karl Broman)
Date: Mon, 30 Sep 2019 20:27:17 +0000
Subject: Re: [Rqtl-disc] How to code NIL genotype in R/qtl?
Message-ID: <egc2GltlKfs.9OcNzVEfCAAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <egc2GltlKfs.QeOxue0XCAAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
References: <egc2GltlKfs.QeOxue0XCAAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl-disc/c/egc2GltlKfs/m/9OcNzVEfCAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

R/qtl doesn't have any specific support for NILs. You could try
importing them as if they were RILs (using crosstype="riself" in
read.cross).

The genotypes can be encoded in a variety of ways but need to indicate
the parental origins of alleles, for example AA/BB or A/B.

karl

